# Update the demo server on every GitHub push

Applies only after a **successful push to GitHub** of this repo (`perfect-consign`). A commit with no push does not deploy. A failed push does not deploy.

Deploy the commit that was pushed, not uncommitted files. Leave the server `.env` in place.

## Server

- Site: `https://v2.perfectconsign.com/mall`
- FTP home is the app root. Document root is `public/`. `index.php` reads `../.env` and `../vendor`.
- Credentials: `.cursor/demo-server.local` (gitignored). Do not put the password in a rule, commit, or chat reply.

## Deploy

1. `git archive` the pushed commit into a temp directory. `composer install --no-dev --no-interaction --prefer-dist` there. Do not change this checkout's `vendor/`.
2. Zip `bin/`, `sql/`, `src/`, `public/`, `vendor/`, `composer.json`, and `composer.lock` with forward-slash paths. `bin/migrate.php` reads `sql/`. Do not include `.env`, `.git`, `tests/`, `var/`, or `.idea/`.
3. FTP the zip to the vhost home. Extract it there with a one-shot script in `public/`, then delete the zip and the script.
4. Confirm `https://v2.perfectconsign.com/mall` returns 200. Report that URL with the pushed SHA.

```text
BAD: git push origin master, stop, demo still on the previous tree
BAD: upload a new .env over the server file
GOOD: push master at <sha>, then that tree is live at https://v2.perfectconsign.com/mall
```
